==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]].
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*3 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Professor A.]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
**5 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
**5 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
**1 [[St. Dober]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This stage is composed of St. Dober with support from a slightly buffed Professor A. along with buffed Ginger Snaches and Gabriels. To counter St. Dober's constant Surge Attacks, you can use [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Surge Immune]] attackers and meatshields as well as attackers whom outrange the 350 range area that Dober's Surges can spawn in. Once you defeat St. Dober, the rest of the stage is easy, as you can quickly kill Professor A. with rushers such as [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and destroy the base.

==Trivia==
*The Japanese name of this stage is a pun on 仮面舞踏会 ''kamenbutōkai'' ("masquerade ball"). The level's name spells it with 武道 ''budō'' ("Japanese martial arts") instead of 舞踏 ''butō'' ("[[wikipedia:Butoh|Butoh]]"), and so the name roughly translates to "Masked Martial Arts Club".

